🔑 Core Date Functions in Spark SQL
current_date → Returns today’s date (no time).

current_timestamp → Returns current date + time at query start.

date_add → Adds days to a given date.

date_sub → Subtracts days from a given date.

add_months → Adds months to a date.

last_day → Returns the last day of the month for a given date.

next_day → Finds the next specified weekday after a date.

datediff → Difference in days between two dates.

months_between → Number of months between two dates.

🕒 Timestamp & Formatting Functions
to_date → Converts string/timestamp to DateType.

to_timestamp → Converts string to TimestampType.

date_format → Formats date/timestamp into a string.

unix_timestamp → Converts date/timestamp to Unix epoch seconds.

from_unixtime → Converts epoch seconds back to timestamp.

convert_timezone → Converts timestamps between time zones (Spark 3.4+).

📊 Extracting Date Components
year, month, dayofmonth → Extract year, month, day.

hour, minute, second → Extract time components.

weekofyear → Returns week number.

quarter → Returns quarter of the year.
